Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 MAY 02 ACCESSIONED ON  24 MAY 02 at 11 01 CLINICAL DATA  42 year old female with history of invasive and in situ ductal carcinoma in the left breast  now with simple mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  RESIDUAL STROMALLY INVASIVE OR IN SITU CARCINOMA IS NOT SEEN  NOTE  One lymph node is replaced by tumor and measures 0 25cm in greatest dimension  Slight extranodal extension is present  The adjacent 0 3cm lymph node contains a 0 05cm metastatic deposit  These two lymph nodes are in the area denoted by the stitch  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  29 MAY 02 at 18 18                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  designated as  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE kilogram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm simple mastectomy oriented by a bow tie designating the axillary end and a suture designating an  alleged tumor or lymph node   The anterior aspect of the specimen is notable for a REMOVED_DATE x 13 0cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm nipple and a 4 5cm well healed scar  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm cavity consistent with previous excisional biopsy  located beneath the scar and 0 2cm from the deep margin  The remainder of the parenchyma is composed of 80  adipose and 20  fibrous tissue  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm firm area is identified in the area marked by the suture  Additional discrete nodules that are easily expressed from the tissue are identified between the stitch and the biopsy site  No lymph nodes are identified in the axillary end marked by the bow tie  Representative sections are submitted  A B  cavity to deep margin C E  cavity and surrounding parenchyma F  cavity G  uninvolved parenchyma H I  area designated by suture  each block representing a bivalved tissue fragment  J L  three nodules  each bivalved  located between cavity and area designated by stitch Resident  SOHEIL DADRAS  MD  PHD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  13 MAY 98 at 10 08 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  15 MAY 98 at 18 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 11 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of soft  tan cores of tissue  which are submitted in toto in Cassette A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Priscilla Slanetz  M D  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Alphonse Taghian  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY , Not_reported.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 MAY 03 ACCESSIONED ON  19 MAY 03 at 11 11 CLINICAL DATA  Positive margin on lumpectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  EXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH A SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASION  SEE TABLE  1  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Involving 12 of 12 blocks  specimen entirely submitted   Grade  1 and focally 2  Calcifications  Limited to the carcinoma in situ  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 2cm from the medial anterior  superior and inferior margins of the specimen in multiple foci and is focally present at the posterior margin  NOTE  The ductal carcinoma cells stain for e cadherin  Myoepithelial cells s tain for smooth muscle actin  myosin  and p63  BREAST  RIGHT   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU SPANNING ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM AND PRESENT IN 2 OF 2 BLOCKS  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 03 at 17 01                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  re excision right breast  short stitch new inferior margin  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregular portion of tan yellow to pink fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating the new inferior margin and a long stitch designating the lateral margin  The entire length of the superior aspect displays tan pink  focally hemorrhagic smooth slightly fibrotic tissue  The inferior margin is inked yellow  the superior green  the anterior blue  the posterior black  The specimen is sequentially sectioned from medial to lateral  The cut surface is pink to white  rubbery to fibrotic  with focal tan yellow areas  consistent with fat necrosis  which abut the green inked superior margin  No discrete masses or lesions are identified  The specimen has been entirely submitted from the medial to lateral aspect sequentially in cassettes A L  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final shaved margins  are 3 0x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm of irregular tan yellow to pink lobulated portions of unoriented fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes M P  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional medial margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregular portion of tan yellow to pink lobulated  unoriented portion of fibroadipose tissue  Along one aspect there is a tan pink  focally hemorrhagic  smooth and fibrotic surface  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes Q R  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  NEW INFERIOR MARGIN  RE EXCISION PART B  BREAST RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN  EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISIO , No.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 45 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY     INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  WITH NEURAL AND POSSIBLE VASCULAR INVASION     DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5       FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SEE NOTE   NOTE  infiltrating carcinoma extends to inked margins and the single focus of ductal carcinoma in situ extends to within less than 0 1cm of an inked resection margin  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 18                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 03     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   9   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fibrofatty piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a well circumscribed  rubbery  tan to yellow nodule abutting all inked surfaces  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  A section was taken for BRDU studies  The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in A and B  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING AND IN SITU CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Suspicious.
